  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The essence of the Void empowers you for the duration, wrapping you in shadow and tinting you dark blue or purple. While the spell lasts, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Preternatural Calm.</strong> You automatically succeed on Constitution saving throws made to maintain Concentration.</p><p><strong>Shadow Shroud.</strong> Shadows cloak you, and your space is &amp;Reference[lightlyobscured apply=false]{Lightly Obscured}.</p><p><strong>Touch of the Void.</strong> Once on each of your turns, when you deal damage to a creature, you can deal an extra 1d4 Necrotic damage to it; or when you heal a creature, you can restore an extra 1d4 Hit Points to it.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The extra damage or healing of Touch of the Void increases by 1d4 for each spell slot level above 1.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-BfBTAWAuqnfUgO8e\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The effect marks you. The Concentration successes and the obscured space are handled by hand; use the Touch of the Void activities, choosing the level you cast the spell at.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
